  "wikitext": "[[Category:Asset]]\nRubber is an asset manufactured in a [[Rubber factory]] and used to build other assets or can be sold. \nSynthetic rubber, like natural rubber, has uses in the automotive industry for tires, door and window profiles, hoses, belts, matting, and flooring.\n\n== Rubber Production ==\n{| class=\"wikitable sortable\"\n!Name !! Cost !! Inputs !! Outputs !! Profit/Min !! Production <br/>interval (MM:SS)\n|-\n|[[Rubber factory]] || $1,500 || 8x [[crude oil]] || 1x [[rubber]] || $9.30 || 0:40\n|-\n|}\n\n== Facilities that use Rubber ==\n{|class=\"wikitable\"\n!Name !! Cost !! Inputs !! Outputs !! Profit/Min !! Production <br/>interval (MM:SS)\n|-\n|[[Bicycle factory]] || $10,000 || 8x [[rubber]], 12x [[steel]] || 1x [[bicycle]] || $58.67~ || 1:30\n|-\n|[[Gasoline engine factory]] || $2,000,000 || 6x [[rubber]], 15x [[steel]] || 1x [[gasoline engine]] || $1,116.46~ || 4:20\n|-\n|[[Car factory]] || $10,000,000 || 30x [[rubber]], 40x [[steel]], 28x [[glass]], 1x [[CPU]], 1x [[gasoline engine]], 1000x [[plastic]] || 1x [[car]] || $1,293.00 || 10:00\n|}",
